  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Isoliquiritigenin may interact with Proto-oncogene tyrosine-protein kinase Src through a series of intermediate targets. Specifically, Isoliquiritigenin is linked to Interleukin-11 receptor subunit alpha, which in turn is targeted by Karenin, Eschweilenol C, and trans-Norbixin. All of these intermediates are known to interact with Proto-oncogene tyrosine-protein kinase Src, indicating a potential pathway through which Isoliquiritigenin could influence the kinase activity of Src. The scores from the three paths, ranging from 0.6332 to 0.6482, suggest a consistent level of confidence in the relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a possible regulatory role for Isoliquiritigenin in the Src signaling pathway, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
